Feature: Calculate actual_value for each brand, country, territory, month, and year by summing sales_value from t3_itm_territory_sales and sales_net_price_local from t3_ttm_territory_sales

  As a data engineer,
  I want to generate a Databricks SQL query that calculates the actual_value for each combination of brand_name, country_code, territory_id, month, and year,
  By summing sales_value from purgo_playground.t3_itm_territory_sales and sales_net_price_local from purgo_playground.t3_ttm_territory_sales,
  Ensuring only records with valid source_system_name in purgo_playground.control_table are included,
  So that the output can be loaded into purgo_playground.actual_value_calculation.

  Background:
    Given the table purgo_playground.t3_itm_territory_sales contains columns: country_code, brand_name, source_system_name, territory_id, sales_value, sales_month
    And the table purgo_playground.t3_ttm_territory_sales contains columns: country_code, brand_name, source_system_name, territory_id, sales_net_price_local, fiscal_date
    And the table purgo_playground.control_table contains columns: country_code, source_system, brand_name
    And the output table purgo_playground.actual_value_calculation requires: country_code (string, not null), brand_name (string, not null), territory_id (string, not null), month (string, not null), year (string, not null), actual_value (double, not null)
    And month and year must be extracted as strings in 'MM' and 'YYYY' format respectively from sales_month and fiscal_date
    And only records where source_system_name from both source tables exist in control_table.source_system are included
    And if a record exists in one source table but not the other, the missing value is treated as zero
    And nulls in sales_value or sales_net_price_local are treated as zero in the sum
    And duplicate records are aggregated by summing their values

  Scenario Outline: Calculate actual_value for valid brand/country/territory/month/year combinations (happy path)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <itm_source>      | <territory>  | <itm_value> | <itm_month>  |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <ttm_source>      | <territory>  | <ttm_value>           | <ttm_month>  |
    And control_table contains
      | source_system | brand_name | country_code |
      | <itm_source>  | <brand>    | <country>    |
      | <ttm_source>  | <brand>    | <country>    |
    When the actual_value calculation query is executed
    Then the output contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | month | year  | actual_value |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <territory>  | <month>| <year>| <expected>   |

    Examples:
      | country   | brand    | territory | itm_source | ttm_source | itm_value | ttm_value | itm_month   | ttm_month   | month | year  | expected |
      | US        | BRANDX   | TID001    | SYS1       | SYS2       | 100.0     | 200.0     | 2023-05-01  | 2023-05-15  | 05    | 2023 | 300.0    |
      | DE        | BRANDY   | TID002    | SYS3       | SYS3       | 50.0      | 75.0      | 2022-12-01  | 2022-12-20  | 12    | 2022 | 125.0    |

  Scenario Outline: Calculate actual_value when only one source table has data (other is missing)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <itm_source>      | <territory>  | <itm_value> | <itm_month>  |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains no matching record for
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | month | year  |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <territory>  | <month>| <year>|
    And control_table contains
      | source_system | brand_name | country_code |
      | <itm_source>  | <brand>    | <country>    |
    When the actual_value calculation query is executed
    Then the output contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | month | year  | actual_value |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <territory>  | <month>| <year>| <expected>   |

    Examples:
      | country   | brand    | territory | itm_source | itm_value | itm_month   | month | year  | expected |
      | US        | BRANDZ   | TID003    | SYS4       | 150.0     | 2023-06-01  | 06    | 2023 | 150.0    |

  Scenario Outline: Calculate actual_value when only t3_ttm_territory_sales has data (other is missing)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains no matching record for
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | month | year  |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <territory>  | <month>| <year>|
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <ttm_source>      | <territory>  | <ttm_value>           | <ttm_month>  |
    And control_table contains
      | source_system | brand_name | country_code |
      | <ttm_source>  | <brand>    | <country>    |
    When the actual_value calculation query is executed
    Then the output contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | month | year  | actual_value |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <territory>  | <month>| <year>| <expected>   |

    Examples:
      | country   | brand    | territory | ttm_source | ttm_value | ttm_month   | month | year  | expected |
      | FR        | BRANDW   | TID004    | SYS5       | 80.0      | 2023-07-10  | 07    | 2023 | 80.0     |

  Scenario Outline: Exclude records where source_system_name is not in control_table (error scenario)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <itm_source>      | <territory>  | <itm_value> | <itm_month>  |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <ttm_source>      | <territory>  | <ttm_value>           | <ttm_month>  |
    And control_table does not contain
      | source_system | brand_name | country_code |
      | <itm_source>  | <brand>    | <country>    |
      | <ttm_source>  | <brand>    | <country>    |
    When the actual_value calculation query is executed
    Then the output does not contain a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | month | year  |

    Examples:
      | country   | brand    | territory | itm_source | ttm_source | itm_value | ttm_value | itm_month   | ttm_month   | month | year  |
      | IT        | BRANDQ   | TID005    | SYS6       | SYS7       | 120.0     | 130.0     | 2023-08-01  | 2023-08-15  | 08    | 2023 |

  Scenario Outline: Null sales_value or sales_net_price_local is treated as zero
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <itm_source>      | <territory>  | <itm_value> | <itm_month>  |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <ttm_source>      | <territory>  | <ttm_value>           | <ttm_month>  |
    And control_table contains
      | source_system | brand_name | country_code |
      | <itm_source>  | <brand>    | <country>    |
      | <ttm_source>  | <brand>    | <country>    |
    When the actual_value calculation query is executed
    Then the output contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | month | year  | actual_value |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <territory>  | <month>| <year>| <expected>   |

    Examples:
      | country   | brand    | territory | itm_source | ttm_source | itm_value | ttm_value | itm_month   | ttm_month   | month | year  | expected |
      | ES        | BRANDN   | TID006    | SYS8       | SYS9       | null      | 90.0      | 2023-09-01  | 2023-09-10  | 09    | 2023 | 90.0     |
      | UK        | BRANDO   | TID007    | SYS10      | SYS11      | 110.0     | null      | 2023-10-01  | 2023-10-20  | 10    | 2023 | 110.0    |
      | NL        | BRANDP   | TID008    | SYS12      | SYS13      | null      | null      | 2023-11-01  | 2023-11-15  | 11    | 2023 | 0.0      |

  Scenario: Output month and year are always two-digit and four-digit strings respectively
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | US           | BRANDM     | SYS14             | TID009       | 200.0       | 2023-01-05   |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | US           | BRANDM     | SYS15             | TID009       | 300.0                 | 2023-01-25   |
    And control_table contains
      | source_system | brand_name | country_code |
      | SYS14         | BRANDM     | US           |
      | SYS15         | BRANDM     | US           |
    When the actual_value calculation query is executed
    Then the output contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | month | year  | actual_value |
      | US           | BRANDM     | TID009       | 01    | 2023 | 500.0        |

  Scenario Outline: Duplicate records are aggregated by summing their values
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains records
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <itm_source>      | <territory>  | <itm_value1>| <itm_month>  |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <itm_source>      | <territory>  | <itm_value2>| <itm_month>  |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains records
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <ttm_source>      | <territory>  | <ttm_value1>         | <ttm_month>  |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <ttm_source>      | <territory>  | <ttm_value2>         | <ttm_month>  |
    And control_table contains
      | source_system | brand_name | country_code |
      | <itm_source>  | <brand>    | <country>    |
      | <ttm_source>  | <brand>    | <country>    |
    When the actual_value calculation query is executed
    Then the output contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | month | year  | actual_value |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <territory>  | <month>| <year>| <expected>   |

    Examples:
      | country   | brand    | territory | itm_source | ttm_source | itm_value1 | itm_value2 | ttm_value1 | ttm_value2 | itm_month   | ttm_month   | month | year  | expected |
      | US        | BRANDD   | TID010    | SYS16      | SYS17      | 50.0       | 70.0       | 30.0       | 20.0       | 2023-02-01  | 2023-02-15  | 02    | 2023 | 170.0    |

  Scenario Outline: Error - Invalid data types or formats in sales_value or sales_net_price_local
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <itm_source>      | <territory>  | <itm_value> | <itm_month>  |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <ttm_source>      | <territory>  | <ttm_value>           | <ttm_month>  |
    And control_table contains
      | source_system | brand_name | country_code |
      | <itm_source>  | <brand>    | <country>    |
      | <ttm_source>  | <brand>    | <country>    |
    When the actual_value calculation query is executed
    Then the output contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | month | year  | actual_value |
      | <country>    | <brand>    | <territory>  | <month>| <year>| <expected>   |
    And any non-numeric sales_value or sales_net_price_local is treated as zero

    Examples:
      | country   | brand    | territory | itm_source | ttm_source | itm_value | ttm_value | itm_month   | ttm_month   | month | year  | expected |
      | US        | BRANDE   | TID011    | SYS18      | SYS19      | 'abc'     | 100.0     | 2023-03-01  | 2023-03-10  | 03    | 2023 | 100.0    |
      | US        | BRANDF   | TID012    | SYS20      | SYS21      | 200.0     | 'xyz'     | 2023-04-01  | 2023-04-10  | 04    | 2023 | 200.0    |
      | US        | BRANDG   | TID013    | SYS22      | SYS23      | 'abc'     | 'xyz'     | 2023-05-01  | 2023-05-10  | 05    | 2023 | 0.0      |

  Scenario: Error - Output must not contain nulls in any required field
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains a record with
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | US           | BRANDH     | SYS24             | TID014       | 100.0       | 2023-06-01   |
